Intercom first desktop voice and context-mesh slice

Workstream ID: ic-06
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Intercom/issues/5
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: One observable voice-to-existing-session-to-spoken-result loop
Dependencies: ic-02, ic-04, ic-05

Purpose:
  Implement the bounded desktop experience only after separate authorization
  and qualification. Tauri 2/Rust + React/TypeScript/Three.js is now the
  product candidate. The owner separately authorized an early fixture-only
  Electron UI, including transparent Floating Mesh, before the live prerequisites.
  Dependencies remain required for the real voice-to-existing-session loop.
  The later request separately authorizes installed local-English push-to-talk
  and conversation-only use of one designated existing idle session. The broader
  orchestrator and wake dependencies remain open. The subsequent complete-slice
  request authorizes actual mesh startup and separately confirmed existing-idle-
  session work with retained permissions. Push-to-talk remains selected.

